{"exhaustive":{"nbHits":false,"typo":false},"exhaustiveNbHits":false,"exhaustiveTypo":false,"hits":[{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"po"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["launched"],"value":"This is great <i>but...</i><p>Systems like Hacker News are great because they are relatively unknown. When a system like this takes off, it puts a lot of pressure on moderation of its source. Is dang ready to moderate an influx of comment spam?<p>Not a criticism at all... just that we're going to see this happening all over the place. It's become very easy to scrape data and <em>launch</em> something. If you are a source for an audience, people will start to game your thing."},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"HackerTube: YouTube built from videos recommended by HN"},"story_url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://karpathy.bearblog.dev/hacker-tube/"}},"_tags":["comment","author_po","story_50319510"],"author":"po","children":[50335025],"comment_text":"This is great <i>but...</i><p>Systems like Hacker News are great because they are relatively unknown. When a system like this takes off, it puts a lot of pressure on moderation of its source. Is dang ready to moderate an influx of comment spam?<p>Not a criticism at all... just that we&#x27;re going to see this happening all over the place. It&#x27;s become very easy to scrape data and launch something. If you are a source for an audience, people will start to game your thing.","created_at":"2026-11-02T10:15:30Z","created_at_i":1793614530,"objectID":"50335000","parent_id":50319510,"story_id":50319510,"story_title":"HackerTube: YouTube built from videos recommended by HN","story_url":"https://karpathy.bearblog.dev/hacker-tube/","updated_at":"2026-11-02T10:47:12Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Joel_Mckay"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["launched"],"value":"Your Bitlocker recovery key is uploaded to the Cloud with either an online account, or one-drive activation.  It is illegal for Microsoft to reject assisting in cracking your machine.<p>What Bitlocker/TPM did accomplish was booby-trapping peoples PC. You are met with the recovery blue-screen if you went through the effort of installing  an offline account, and tried to dual boot off the same physical drive. No one is told to backup your recovery key post install, and so the incentive to always use their shitty cloud options is encouraged with data loss.<p>Note too, NTFS will have encryption auto-enabled on anything you plug into Windows 11. Note, post-install it is non-trivial to fix the troublesome behavior.<p>Rufus is now the only way to install Windows 11 pro without the enshittification features:<p><a href=\"https://github.com/pbatard/rufus/releases\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://github.com/pbatard/rufus/releases</a><p>Ripping out all the &quot;AI&quot; (undocumented API areas indicate snitch-ware), spam, and telemetry nonsense takes some effort. However, the only thing that should be running on windows now is the Steam <em>launcher</em> for classic games, and a tool to neuter most of the Microsoft malware.<p><a href=\"https://www.oo-software.com/en/shutup10\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.oo-software.com/en/shutup10</a><p>It is sad, but Microsoft has some people willing to burn company goodwill for short-term gains.  Even xbox now sucks, and that was easy money. =3"},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Lenovo's 'encrypted' fingerprint USB is just an unencrypted SD card in a case"},"story_url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://www.reddit.com/r/technology/comments/1xl2pr3/lenovos_encrypted_fingerprint_usb_drive_is_just/"}},"_tags":["comment","author_Joel_Mckay","story_50326099"],"author":"Joel_Mckay","comment_text":"Your Bitlocker recovery key is uploaded to the Cloud with either an online account, or one-drive activation.  It is illegal for Microsoft to reject assisting in cracking your machine.<p>What Bitlocker&#x2F;TPM did accomplish was booby-trapping peoples PC. You are met with the recovery blue-screen if you went through the effort of installing  an offline account, and tried to dual boot off the same physical drive. No one is told to backup your recovery key post install, and so the incentive to always use their shitty cloud options is encouraged with data loss.<p>Note too, NTFS will have encryption auto-enabled on anything you plug into Windows 11. Note, post-install it is non-trivial to fix the troublesome behavior.<p>Rufus is now the only way to install Windows 11 pro without the enshittification features:<p><a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;pbatard&#x2F;rufus&#x2F;releases\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;pbatard&#x2F;rufus&#x2F;releases</a><p>Ripping out all the &quot;AI&quot; (undocumented API areas indicate snitch-ware), spam, and telemetry nonsense takes some effort. However, the only thing that should be running on windows now is the Steam launcher for classic games, and a tool to neuter most of the Microsoft malware.<p><a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.oo-software.com&#x2F;en&#x2F;shutup10\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.oo-software.com&#x2F;en&#x2F;shutup10</a><p>It is sad, but Microsoft has some people willing to burn company goodwill for short-term gains.  Even xbox now sucks, and that was easy money. =3","created_at":"2026-11-02T09:54:35Z","created_at_i":1793613275,"objectID":"50334867","parent_id":50326710,"story_id":50326099,"story_title":"Lenovo's 'encrypted' fingerprint USB is just an unencrypted SD card in a case","story_url":"https://www.reddit.com/r/technology/comments/1xl2pr3/lenovos_encrypted_fingerprint_usb_drive_is_just/","updated_at":"2026-11-02T10:00:12Z"}],"hitsPerPage":2,"nbHits":1706,"nbPages":500,"page":0,"params":"query=launched&tags=%28comment%2Cshow_hn%